  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 127 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nA persistent typical early August forecast is expected for rest of \nthe week into the weekend. Mid-level ridging centered over the \nDesert Southwest elongates, allowing for a slight rise in 500 mb \nheights locally across our region. The low-level pattern with weak \nsurface high pressure stretching across the gulf will maintain a \nlight to moderate south-southeasterly off the gulf. This allows the \ndew points to return to what we are used to for this time of year \nand the typical cycle for development of low clouds each morning \nbreaking into mostly sunny skies in the afternoon. Majority remain \nrain free for the period, with the exception of our southeastern \ncoastal plain counties, where an isolated sea breeze shower and/or \nstorm may be able to reach into during any of the afternoons from \nFriday into the weekend. Temperatures should trend as one would \nexpect for the hottest time of the year featuring highs in the mid \nto upper 90s with higher peak heat indices up to as high as 107 \ndegrees while the overnight lows run in the mid to upper 70s.",
